Miasma npm Credential Harvester: Node.js Accessing Sensitive Credentials

This threat hunting scenario focuses on detecting suspicious credential-harvesting activity involving Node.js or Bun runtimes. The hunt identifies node.exe or bun.exe processes accessing sensitive files and directories that may contain authentication material, such as .npmrc, .aws/credentials, .ssh, .kube/config, Docker credentials, and Claude/API configuration files. These locations can contain tokens, API keys, private keys, registry credentials, and cloud authentication data.

The investigation also looks for Node.js/Bun processes executing commands or scripts associated with credential discovery, collection, or automated data gathering, particularly when the runtime is launched from unusual directories or by unexpected parent processes. Correlating sensitive file access with subsequent archive creation, encoded data, outbound network connections, or suspicious external destinations can help identify potential credential theft and exfiltration from compromised development environments.

T1552.001 – Unsecured Credentials: Credentials In Files
T1552.004 – Unsecured Credentials: Private Keys

Cortex:

dataset = xdr_data
| filter actor_process_image_name in ("node", "node.exe")
| filter
    (event_type = ENUM.FILE and
     action_file_path ~= "(?i)(\\.aws[/\\\\](credentials|config)|\\.config[/\\\\]gcloud|\\.azure[/\\\\]|application_default_credentials\\.json|service_account\\.json)")
    or
    (event_type = ENUM.NETWORK and
     action_remote_ip = "85.137.53.71" and
     action_remote_port in (8080, 8081))
| fields _time, agent_hostname, event_type,
         actor_process_image_name, actor_process_image_path,
         actor_process_command_line,
         action_file_path, action_file_name,
         action_remote_ip, action_remote_port
| sort desc _time
| limit 100
